# 5. Data Flow Thinking

# Process Chosen: Student Registration

---

# UI

Student fills registration form using LWC components.

Fields:
- Name
- Email
- Course
- Phone Number

---

# Validation

Validation Rules check:
- Required fields
- Duplicate email
- Correct phone format
- Course seat availability

If invalid:
- Error message displayed

---

# Flow

Salesforce Flow performs:
- Course allocation
- Welcome task creation
- Student onboarding process

---

# Apex

Apex Trigger executes:
- Create student ID
- Update dashboards
- Generate notifications
- Handle complex business logic

---

# Database

Salesforce stores:
- Student details
- Course details
- Registration records
- Activity logs

---

# Notification

System sends:
- Registration confirmation email
- Faculty notification
- SMS confirmation
- Dashboard alerts

---

# Complete Data Flow Diagram

```text
Student UI
   ↓
Validation Rules
   ↓
Salesforce Flow
   ↓
Apex Trigger
   ↓
Salesforce Database
   ↓
Notifications & Dashboard Updates
```

---

# Conclusion

Modern Salesforce enterprise applications use Lightning Web Components, modular architecture, automation flows, Apex logic, and secure dashboards to create scalable and efficient systems. Proper architecture improves performance, maintainability, teamwork, and user experience.
